  "featureGroup": false,
  "description": "The \u0027dss_plugins_cached\u0027 dataset provides a comprehensive overview of various plugins used within a system, capturing essential details such as unique identifiers, human-readable names, version numbers, authorship, and more. This dataset is particularly useful for managing and tracking plugins, ensuring that users can easily identify and update them as needed. Each plugin is uniquely identified by an \u0027id\u0027, and further described by a \u0027label\u0027 which provides a more user-friendly name. The \u0027version\u0027 column helps in tracking updates and ensuring compatibility. Authorship is captured in the \u0027author\u0027 column, providing credit and a point of contact for each plugin. The \u0027tags\u0027 column aids in categorization, making it easier to search and filter plugins based on keywords. A detailed \u0027description\u0027 of each plugin\u0027s functionality is provided, offering insights into its capabilities and use cases. The \u0027isDev\u0027 column indicates whether a plugin is still in development, which is crucial for users who need stable releases. Finally, the \u0027url\u0027 column provides direct access to more information about each plugin, facilitating further exploration and understanding. This dataset is invaluable for developers, system administrators, and users who need to manage and utilize plugins effectively.",
  "shortDesc": "Dataset of cached plugins with details like ID, version, and author.",
